@page "/"

<PageTitle>StudySync</PageTitle>

<section class="hero">
    <div class="hero-copy">
        <span class="eyebrow">CSE 325 Group Project</span>
        <h1>Study better, together.</h1>
        <p class="lead">StudySync helps college students discover course-specific study groups, organize focused sessions, and keep their academic collaboration in one place.</p>
        <div class="hero-actions">
            <a class="btn btn-primary btn-lg" href="#features">Explore the proposal</a>
            <a class="btn btn-outline-secondary btn-lg" href="https://github.com/VictorChavez0501/CSE325-Group-Project" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">View GitHub</a>
        </div>
    </div>
    <aside class="project-card" aria-label="Project status">
        <span class="status">Week 03 · Proposal</span>
        <h2>Semester MVP</h2>
        <p>A responsive Blazor application focused on reliable group discovery and session scheduling.</p>
        <dl>
            <div><dt>Platform</dt><dd>Web</dd></div>
            <div><dt>Framework</dt><dd>ASP.NET Core Blazor</dd></div>
            <div><dt>Team</dt><dd>4 developers</dd></div>
        </dl>
    </aside>
</section>

<section class="section" id="features">
    <div class="section-heading">
        <span class="eyebrow">Planned experience</span>
        <h2>Core features</h2>
        <p>The proposal intentionally limits the first release to seven clear, achievable workflows.</p>
    </div>
    <div class="feature-grid">
        <article><span>01</span><h3>Secure accounts</h3><p>Students register and sign in to manage their own activity.</p></article>
        <article><span>02</span><h3>Student profiles</h3><p>Members share a display name and academic interests.</p></article>
        <article><span>03</span><h3>Study groups</h3><p>Students create and manage groups connected to a course.</p></article>
        <article><span>04</span><h3>Group discovery</h3><p>Search and filters make relevant groups easy to find.</p></article>
        <article><span>05</span><h3>Session scheduling</h3><p>Owners publish a topic, time, location, and capacity.</p></article>
        <article><span>06</span><h3>Attendance</h3><p>Students join or leave sessions with available space.</p></article>
        <article><span>07</span><h3>Personal dashboard</h3><p>Upcoming sessions and memberships appear in one view.</p></article>
    </div>
</section>

<section class="scope-section">
    <div>
        <span class="eyebrow">Built for focus</span>
        <h2>A realistic semester scope</h2>
    </div>
    <p>The first release will emphasize authentication, relational data, authorization, validation, and responsive design. Real-time chat, video calls, notifications, payments, and university-system integrations remain outside the MVP.</p>
</section>
